---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import TimeLineElement from "../components/cv/TimeLine.astro";
import Jobtitle from "../components/cv/Jobtitle.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Resume">
  <div class="relative bg-white text-gray-900 font-serif shadow-xl rounded-md mx-auto max-w-[850px] p-6 sm:p-10">
    <a
      href="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ZaheerUdDeen/portfolio/main/public/resume.pdf"
      download
      id="downloadButton"
      title="Download PDF"
      class="absolute top-4 right-4 sm:top-6 sm:right-6 text-gray-500 hover:text-gray-800"
    >
      <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="20" height="20" fill="currentColor"><path d="M12 16l-6-6h4V4h4v6h4l-6 6zm-7 2h14v2H5v-2z"/></svg>
    </a>

    <div class="text-center mb-4">
      <div class="text-3xl font-bold">Zaheer Ud Din</div>
      <div class="text-lg text-gray-700">Staff Consultant Engineer · AI-Native Software Engineering</div>
      <div class="text-sm text-gray-600 mt-1 flex flex-wrap items-baseline justify-center gap-x-2">
        <span>+92-311-5076756</span>
        <span>|</span>
        <span>zaheeru7@gmail.com</span>
        <span>|</span>
        <span>Islamabad, Pakistan</span>
      </div>
      <div class="text-sm mt-1 flex flex-wrap items-baseline justify-center gap-x-2">
        <a href="https://linkedin.com/in/zaheeru7" target="_blank" class="text-blue-700 hover:underline">linkedin.com/in/zaheeru7</a>
        <span>|</span>
        <a href="https://github.com/zaheeruddeen" target="_blank" class="text-blue-700 hover:underline">github.com/zaheeruddeen</a>
        <span>|</span>
        <a href="https://zaheeruddeen.github.io/portfolio" target="_blank" class="text-blue-700 hover:underline">zaheeruddeen.github.io/portfolio</a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <hr class="border-gray-400 mb-5" />

    <div class="text-lg font-bold uppercase tracking-wide">Professional Summary</div>
    <hr class="border-gray-400 mb-3" />
    <div class="text-sm text-justify mb-6">
      AI-native staff engineer with 8+ years shipping production systems. I build with Claude Code and
      Cursor every day, and I build AI into the products themselves: agentic LLM workflows with tool
      calling (MCP), guardrails, evals and human-in-the-loop review. At DNext (client: STC) I built an
      agent that converts arbitrary Excel product catalogues into STC's template format, alongside
      the Kafka/Camunda engine that federates catalog and identity events across OSS/BSS systems.
      Earlier, I automated BILL.com billing end to end and
      led the Global Rescue platform revamp that Fast Company recognized as one of 2024's most
      innovative products. Outside work, I run PerFinAI, an AI-native finance assistant that is
      largely built and maintained by agents inside a harness I designed. I lead small teams, ship
      systems other teams depend on, and make the engineers around me faster.
    </div>

    <div class="text-lg font-bold uppercase tracking-wide">Core Competencies</div>
    <hr class="border-gray-400 mb-3" />
    <ul class="list-disc mx-5 text-sm space-y-1 mb-6">
      <li>
        <span class="font-bold">AI-Assisted Engineering:</span>
        Claude Code (CLAUDE.md context hierarchy, custom skills &amp; slash commands, subagents, hooks,
        permission guardrails, worktree-parallel agents), Cursor (agent mode, rules), spec-first / test-first
        agent loops, fresh-context AI code review, ADR-driven decisions
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="font-bold">Applied AI &amp; Agents:</span>
        LLM agents &amp; agentic workflows, tool calling &amp; MCP, Anthropic API &amp; Claude Agent SDK,
        schema-forced structured outputs, RAG (embeddings, vector search), prompt engineering,
        golden-dataset evals, guardrails, human-in-the-loop, LLM cost governance, OpenTelemetry tracing
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="font-bold">Languages, Frameworks & Frontend:</span>
        Java 8/17/21/25, Spring Boot, Micronaut, TypeScript/Node.js, Python/FastAPI, React 19, Angular Micro-Frontends
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="font-bold">Cloud, Containers & CI/CD:</span>
        AWS (Lambda, ECS/Fargate, RDS, S3, KMS), Docker, Kubernetes, Jenkins, CI/CD Automation
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="font-bold">Data & Messaging:</span>
        Oracle, PostgreSQL, MySQL, MongoDB, DynamoDB, Kafka, RabbitMQ, SQS/SNS
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="font-bold">Architecture & Security:</span>
        Event-Driven & Serverless Architecture, OAuth 2.0, OIDC/SAML, Keycloak
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="font-bold">Testing, Observability & Practices:</span>
        JUnit 5, Mockito, TestContainers, Datadog, Splunk Cloud, Agile/Scrum, Kanban, Sprint Planning
      </li>
    </ul>

    <div class="text-lg font-bold uppercase tracking-wide">Professional Experience</div>
    <hr class="border-gray-400 mb-3" />

    <div class="mb-6">
      <Jobtitle
        title="Staff Software Consultant"
        companyName="DNext"
        companyDescription=" — Client: STC (Saudi Telecommunications, BSS/OSS Federation)"
        fromDate="Jul 2026"
        toDate="Present"
      >
        <p class="italic mb-2">
          Tech: Java, Spring Boot, Apache Kafka, Avro (Confluent Schema Registry), Camunda 7 (BPMN),
          Keycloak, Angular, PostgreSQL, MongoDB, Docker, TypeScript/Node.js, LLM Agents (MCP)
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc mx-5">
          <li class="mb-1 text-justify">
            STC's BSS/OSS synchronization engine federates product-catalog changes from the master
            product catalogue out to downstream systems — CPQ (Configure, Price, Quote), ECOM
            (E-Commerce channel, via Ericsson Catalog Manager), and OCS (Online Charging System,
            Ericsson). Orchestrates the flow through Camunda BPMN workflows.
          </li>
          <li class="mb-1 text-justify">
            Ramping into the engine's event-processing pipeline: contributed to sequencing of
            event-group processing, and added Avro-schema Kafka topic integration for user onboarding
            and role-assignment events, extending the existing publish/listener flow to carry identity
            and access-lifecycle events through the same federation pipeline.
          </li>
        <li class="mb-1 text-justify">
            Built an agentic LLM workflow (TypeScript/Node.js, tool calling via MCP) that converts
            arbitrary Excel product catalogues into STC's UPT template format, with validation in the
            loop, bounded retries, guardrails against invented data, and a human-in-the-loop review
            manifest.
          </li>
          <li class="mb-1 text-justify">
            Built the UPT validation service (Java 25, Spring Boot 4, MongoDB, JSLT): rule-based
            validation of catalogue payloads against product definitions, with configurable
            exceptions, bulk runs and audit history.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </Jobtitle>

      <Jobtitle
        title="Staff Consultant Engineer"
        companyName="10Pearls"
        companyLink="https://www.10pearls.com/"
        companyDescription=" — Client: BILL.com (US Fintech, AP/AR Automation)"
        fromDate="Dec 2025"
        toDate="Jul 2026"
      >
        <p class="italic mb-2">
          Tech: Java 17+, Micronaut 4, Kafka, Flink, AWS (ECS/Fargate, RDS, S3, SQS/SNS, KMS),
          Angular/React 19, Docker, Datadog, Splunk Cloud
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc mx-5">
          <li class="mb-1 text-justify">
            Closed a gap where customers on BILL.com's Supplier Payments Plus were getting invoices but
            no email statements: designed and shipped an end-to-end notification pipeline using an
            async outbox + CDC + Kafka + Flink pattern, delivering automated PDF billing statements
            with zero-loss delivery and zero manual intervention.
          </li>
          <li class="mb-1 text-justify">
            Owned the pipeline end to end — recipient lookup, template assembly, PDF generation, secure
            S3 upload — and established the data boundary between the Billing Engine and Billing
            Facade, resolving a recurring source of cross-team integration friction.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </Jobtitle>

      <Jobtitle
        title="Senior Software Engineer & Team Lead"
        companyName="Global Rescue LLC"
        companyLink="https://www.globalrescue.com/"
        companyDescription=" (US SaaS — Travel Risk & Crisis Management)"
        fromDate="Mar 2022"
        toDate="Nov 2025"
      >
        <p class="italic mb-2">
          Tech: Java 21, Spring Boot 3, Node.js, AWS (ECS, Lambda, API Gateway, DynamoDB, S3, SQS, SNS,
          SES), MySQL, Redis, Elasticsearch, RabbitMQ, Keycloak, Datadog, TestContainers
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc mx-5">
          <li class="mb-1 text-justify">
            When I joined, Global Rescue was running on an aging monolith that couldn't keep up with
            the business. Over 3.5 years, I spearheaded the GRID 2.0 revamp that broke it into
            microservices. Customer renewals jumped after the beta, and Fast Company put Global Rescue
            on its Most Innovative Companies list in 2024 — recognition specifically tied to the system
            we rebuilt.
          </li>
          <li class="mb-1 text-justify">
            Led a team of 6 engineers. I set architectural direction, ran
            design reviews, mentored mid-level engineers into senior roles, and bridged US product
            leadership and our distributed team.
          </li>
          <li class="mb-1 text-justify">
            I consolidated three separate authentication flows into a single identity layer — OAuth 2.0 + OIDC via Keycloak with custom
            SSO support, API Gateway integration, and backward compatibility through dynamic proxies.
            One system instead of three.
          </li>
          <li class="mb-1 text-justify">
            Built the internal platform libraries that other teams now depend on: an auth SDK, a
            circuit-breaker messaging layer, and a unified notification service for email, push, and
            SMS.
          </li>
          <li class="mb-1 text-justify">
            Created a custom monitoring system for the company's most critical API (SOS emergency
            calls). My integration-testing framework
            with synthetic monitoring caught regressions before they hit production.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </Jobtitle>

      <Jobtitle
        title="Software Engineer"
        companyName="Stella Technologies"
        companyLink="https://stellatechnology.com/"
        companyDescription=" (US Digital Healthcare — Silicon Valley)"
        fromDate="Mar 2021"
        toDate="Mar 2022"
      >
        <p class="italic mb-2">
          Tech: Java, Spring Boot, Node.js, AWS Lambda, Step Functions, S3, PostgreSQL, Sequelize ORM
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc mx-5">
          <li class="mb-1 text-justify">
            Stella had a healthcare platform that could talk to its own database but not to anyone
            else's. I engineered the HL7 & FHIR interoperability layer that opened it up to outside
            systems — unlocking data exchange partnerships that became a new revenue stream.
          </li>
          <li class="mb-1 text-justify">
            Replaced a fragile cron-based data pipeline with serverless ETL on AWS Lambda and Step
            Functions. Data latency dropped from hours to near real time, and the on-call team stopped
            getting paged for pipeline failures.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </Jobtitle>

      <Jobtitle
        title="Software Engineer"
        companyName="Zong"
        companyLink="https://www.zong.com.pk/about-zong/china-mobile-pakistan/"
        companyDescription=" — China Mobile Pakistan (Telecom), Islamabad"
        fromDate="Apr 2020"
        toDate="Mar 2021"
      >
        <p class="italic mb-2">Tech: Node.js, PostgreSQL, Sequelize ORM</p>
        <ul class="list-disc mx-5">
          <li class="mb-1 text-justify">
            Took the AutoKiosk Machine from whiteboard to production for one of Pakistan's largest
            telecom providers. Owned planning, building, testing, and go-live.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </Jobtitle>

      <Jobtitle
        title="Software Engineer"
        companyName="Infinium Digital"
        companyLink="https://www.tajdigitalhealth.com/"
        companyDescription=" — TAJ Digital Healthcare, Islamabad"
        fromDate="Jul 2018"
        toDate="Mar 2020"
      >
        <p class="italic mb-2">Tech: Java, Spring Boot, MySQL, AWS (EC2, RDS), Jenkins, OAuth, REST APIs</p>
        <ul class="list-disc mx-5">
          <li class="mb-1 text-justify">
            Joined as a junior; left as the primary backend engineer. Built TAJ's digital healthcare
            platform from an MVP into a fully operational business within a year — the product that
            taught me what it means to own something end to end.
          </li>
          <li class="mb-1 text-justify">
            Designed a referral engine that went viral on launch day: 10,000+ downloads in the first
            release, becoming the product's main growth channel before any paid marketing.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </Jobtitle>
    </div>

    <div class="text-lg font-bold uppercase tracking-wide">AI Projects</div>
    <hr class="border-gray-400 mb-3" />
    <div class="mb-6">
      <Jobtitle
        title="PerFinAI — AI-Native Personal Finance Assistant"
        companyName="Personal project"
        companyDescription=" — agent-built and agent-maintained with Claude Code"
        fromDate="Feb 2026"
        toDate="Present"
      >
        <p class="italic mb-2">
          Tech: Python, FastAPI, Anthropic API, Claude Agent SDK, Claude Code, SQLAlchemy, PostgreSQL,
          React, OpenTelemetry
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc mx-5">
          <li class="mb-1 text-justify">
            Designed a Claude Code development harness so agents do most of the building: a manifest-driven
            module map, a slim CLAUDE.md hierarchy, custom skills (/run-evals, /deliver, /orchestrate,
            /new-adr), planner and fresh-context verifier subagents, and hooks that block writes to
            protected paths and gate completion on tests.
          </li>
          <li class="mb-1 text-justify">
            Built the product on an LLM agent loop with schema-forced tool use, retrieval over embeddings,
            LLM-first categorization with learned exemplars, and agent-authored, self-tested PDF statement
            parsers, all gated by golden-dataset evals, with tenant isolation, LLM cost controls, human
            confirmation before writes, and 70+ architecture decision records.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </Jobtitle>
    </div>

    <div class="text-lg font-bold uppercase tracking-wide">Education</div>
    <hr class="border-gray-400 mb-3" />
    <div class="mb-6">
      <TimeLineElement
        title="Bachelor of Software Engineering — Bahria University, Islamabad"
        subtitle="2014 – 2018"
      />
    </div>

    <div class="text-lg font-bold uppercase tracking-wide">Awards, Entrepreneurship & Additional</div>
    <hr class="border-gray-400 mb-3" />
    <ul class="list-disc mx-5 text-sm space-y-1">
      <li>Winner, HEC Blockchain Hackathon 2018; 1st Place, Bahria Open House 2018.</li>
      <li>Founded Pharmaconn (healthcare startup, won YES Competition). Co-founded Porter ($20K pre-seed). English, Urdu.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
